[{:adr/pattern-4920 "sealed FreightOps-LLM + independent Freight Governor + append-only audit ledger, modeled on the SAME governed-actor architecture as the 87 other prior actors; EIGHTY-EIGHTH actor in this fleet (87 implemented before this build). Third build in the gftdcojp-origin-registry scope extension (after ictrepair/9511 and retailops/4711)", :adr/related ["2607071849-cloud-itonami-repairshop-9521-coverage" "2607087400-cloud-itonami-leathergoods-9523-coverage" "2607091400-cloud-itonami-ictrepair-9511-coverage" "2607091600-cloud-itonami-retailops-4711-coverage" "2607032000-cloud-itonami-insurance-real-estate-coverage" "cloud-itonami-isic-6511 through 4711 ADR-0001s (87 prior actors)" "langgraph ADR-0001" "kotoba-lang/logistics (the capability library this build wraps)"], :adr/status :accepted, :adr/id "2607091700", :adr/scoped-down-r0-4920 "this R0 build deliberately scopes DOWN from the full Decision Rule already published: multi-modal route optimization (the :optimization capability, correctly required) is left as a follow-up slice, not built in this commit", :adr/fleet-maturity-before "{:implemented 87, :blueprint 11, :spec 545, :total 643}", :adr/next-vertical-selection-unconstrained true, :adr/entity-shape-4920 "unlike retailops/4711's own order entity (distinguished by :kind, alternative sale-or-reorder actions), this vertical's dispatch and settle actuation events apply SEQUENTIALLY to the SAME shipment entity -- dispatch first, settlement later -- matching the repair-shop cluster's own sequential ticket shape more closely than retailops's own alternative-kind shape. high-stakes is #{:actuation/dispatch-shipment :actuation/settle-consignment}", :adr/lesson-applied-proactively-4920 "each new check (tracking-number-invalid, pod-chain-integrity-broken, cargo-liability-disclosure-unconfirmed, delivery-exception-unresolved) is exercised directly via its own dedicated demo shipment and test, never only via a happy-path actuation -- applying parksafety's ADR